---
description: "Vite + React project conventions and placement (frontend/)."
globs: "frontend/**/*.ts,frontend/**/*.tsx,frontend/**/*.js,frontend/**/*.jsx"
alwaysApply: false
---

Project rules:
- This is React (Vite), not Next.js. Do not use Next-specific patterns (layout.tsx, server components, metadata exports).
- Prefer feature-based architecture:
  - `frontend/src/pages/` for route-level screens
  - `frontend/src/features/` for domain logic + UI
  - `frontend/src/components/` for reusable components
  - `frontend/src/lib/` for utilities and shared helpers
  - `frontend/src/types/` for shared TypeScript types

Routing:
- If routing is required, ask the user before adding react-router.
- If routing is not required, keep it as a single-page view with internal tabs/sections.

Data fetching:
- Prefer using native fetch with a thin wrapper in `frontend/src/lib/apiClient.ts` unless user approves axios.
